It is worth turning that spoken rule into a simple bookkeeping relation. Let $Y_t$ be income in year $t$, $C_t$ consumption, and $S_t$ investable surplus. The rule is $\begin{aligned}
C_t &\approx Y_{t-5}, \\
S_t &= Y_t - C_t.\end{aligned}$ Substituting the first line into the second, we obtain $S_t \approx Y_t - Y_{t-5}.$

