Let $A$ denote the acquisition price of the business, $E_0$ the initial cash equity check, $L$ the borrowed capital, and $d$ the down-payment fraction. Then $\begin{aligned}
L &= A - E_0, \\
d &= \frac{E_0}{A}.\end{aligned}$

